I just thought of this word and would like to know what you think. There's 
already "ctuji'e" for "parasite", but I think "mivzdacti" may capture the 
meaning better: x1 eats x2, which is the living house of x1. Although I can 
think of a parasite (hemiparasite, actually) which doesn't fit that definition: 
sandalwood pulls sap from the roots of its neighbors, but does not live in 
them.

